    '- Experience within roughly the last 5-6 years carries the most weight. Progressively discount experience older than ~6 years.',
    '- The candidate\'s most-recent role gets a recency uplift even if its tenure is thin, BUT only for RELEVANT (Tier-1/Tier-2) recent work — it signals current direction and fresh skills, so prioritize relevant recent proof above older thin proof and never dismiss it. Off-core recent work (e.g. a Tier-4 role) does NOT lift domain fit; it only shows current activity.',
    '- This uplift does not override the tenure rule: a thin recent role still cannot by itself anchor P01-P03. Depth wins for anchoring (a ~4-year role outranks a ~6-month recent stint); recency wins for tie-breaking and positioning.',
