    '- When a JD maps to several distinct, credible proof points, or to proof spanning more than one relevant role, treat it as stronger than a single-point hit: push toward the top of the allowed bucket. (Any BUCKET-level uplift for this is the SAME lever as SCARCE-ASSET MAPPING below — apply it at most ONCE; convergence and asset-mapping never stack to +2.)',
    '- Weight convergence by credibility: anchor/supporting proofs count fully; stacking multiple thin proofs does NOT substitute for a missing anchor and cannot lift into P01-P03.',
