    '',
    'Seniority fit (two-sided):',
    '- Penalize the gap between the candidate\'s proven level and the role\'s implied level in both directions.',
    '- Over-qualified means a GENUINE 2+ band gap (e.g. a Senior-PM for an APM / entry / new-grad role) — that reduces hire odds (flight-risk / comp-mismatch) and is not a top bucket. A half-step (Senior-PM applying to a plain "PM" role) is NOT over-qualified: it is on-band per the LEVEL CHECK and stays eligible for the top buckets.',
    '- Under-qualified (role clearly above demonstrated scope) reduces hire odds.',
    '- Best odds when the role\'s implied level matches the candidate\'s proven level (PM / Senior PM).',
    '',
    'Differentiation and scarcity:',
    '- Reward rare, hard-to-replicate proof few applicants would have — it raises hire odds.',
    '- Penalize generic matches many applicants meet equally — lower hire odds even when keywords align. Qualified is not the same as standout.',
    '',
    'The stand-out self-check (run this BEFORE assigning P01-P03) — you still judge "would I HIRE", but hiring runs through a shortlist, so the bar differs by bucket:',
    'Picture ~10 other strong fintech/identity PMs from the candidate\'s peer set applying to THIS exact role. P01 = the candidate would be the TOP pick (top ~1 of 10-14) — the rare Tier-1 bullseye where their hard-to-replicate background clearly beats the field. P02-P03 = the candidate is clearly among the STRONGEST FEW the hiring manager would seriously consider and shortlist to hire from (top ~3 of 10) — competitive, not necessarily the single winner. If the honest answer is "qualified, but many others are equally so," the job is P04 — NOT P01-P03. A generic payments, authentication, or platform PM role does NOT clear the P01 bar. Only about 1 in 14 pre-filtered jobs should be P01; if most feel like P01, your bar is too low — raise it.',
    '',
    'Priority buckets (re-centered for a pre-filtered pool — P04 is the default, not P01):',
    '- P01 (rare, ~top 6-8%): TIER-1 BULLSEYE ONLY — the role\'s core is identity verification, eKYC, document/biometric/liveness, anti-deepfake, ID-tampering/document fraud, OR the real-time risk-decisioning rule engine on top of identity & fraud — matched to a STRONGEST anchor proof + PM or Senior-PM IC level + clear product ownership + reliable first-party JD + a real scarcity signal. The role\'s COMPANY-NORMALIZED level must resolve to PM or Senior-PM IC (or banking-VP IC equivalent): a Staff/Lead-titled role that normalizes to Senior-PM scope CAN qualify, but a genuinely Staff/Principal/Group-PM/Director/VP+ SCOPE cannot — apply the graduated bucket demotion, so P01-P03 always end up requiring a PM/Senior-PM IC-level scope. A pure payment-authentication, pure transaction-fraud, pure AML, or pure API/platform role WITHOUT the identity/fraud core does NOT qualify for P01. Score 90-100.',
    '- P02 (~12%): very strong — Tier-1 with one minor gap, OR Tier-2 strong overlap (payment auth, ATO, behavioral biometrics, transaction fraud, AML) that ALSO clearly touches identity/fraud, with strong anchor proof. Score 84-89.',
