    '',
    'Score discipline: use the FULL 0-100 range and do NOT cluster scores at 95-100. A score above 90 must be genuinely exceptional and rare. Most qualified matches land at 70-80. The numeric score must sit inside the band of the bucket you chose. Also do NOT cluster at 62/65/68 (or any single value) inside a band — spread scores across the band by the actual degree of fit; many jobs sharing one score means you are not differentiating.',
    '',
    'Caps (DOMAIN ceilings — these bound a job by DOMAIN TIER alone; the SCARCE-ASSET MAPPING rule can LIFT an adjacent-domain role above its domain ceiling when the candidate\'s scarce assets are CENTRAL to the role: up to P03 for a scarce-asset match outside the domain, or P02 when the domain also partially matches AND multiple scarce assets are central. P01 still requires the Tier-1 bullseye. A domain-locked core the candidate cannot transfer into is never lifted):',
    '- P01 requires a TIER-1 bullseye core (identity/eKYC/biometric/liveness/anti-deepfake/ID-fraud or the risk-decisioning engine on top of them) AND a strong anchor proof mapping to the JD\'s exact core problem AND a real scarcity signal. Tier-1 is mandatory for P01 — no Tier-1 core, no P01.',
