    '- If proof is weak, max P07.',
    '- Famous company alone gives NO uplift; max P04.',
    '- Financial-institution customer segment does not make the product fintech; do not treat it as direct domain.',
    'SCARCE-ASSET MAPPING (the PRIMARY lens for ADJACENT-domain roles — score by matching the candidate\'s SCARCE assets to what THIS JD prizes, not by domain label alone): the candidate\'s hard-to-replicate assets are in the profile\'s SCARCE / DIFFERENTIATING ASSETS list. For each JD: (1) identify its CORE needs plus any explicitly prized/required qualifications (technical background, enterprise experience, MBA, 0-to-1, scale, a specific skill like computer vision); (2) map how many of the candidate\'s SCARCE assets land on those core/high-value needs, WEIGHTED BY CENTRALITY — an asset the role is built around counts fully, a peripheral mention counts little; (3) score by coverage: 2+ scarce assets central -> P02-P03; one scarce asset covering the core -> P03-P04; peripheral-only -> P04-P05. Map SKILL PRIMITIVES, not domain labels — computer-vision, applied-ML, model-eval, risk-decisioning, platform-at-scale, B2B-enterprise, P&L, and technical depth are first-class matchable assets, so a CV/ML/platform/decisioning role reads as core-relevant even outside identity. GUARDRAILS: an asset counts only when CENTRAL; generic overlap most applicants have ("has used AI", basic PM craft) is NOT scarce and earns nothing; a role whose CORE is a domain the candidate cannot transfer into (FX/treasury mechanics, Web3/DLT/crypto, clinical/healthcare-delivery, robotics/simulation, deep logistics) stays P05 no matter how many peripheral assets match. Record the read in why (e.g. "central scarce assets: computer-vision + ML-at-scale + technical; core-relevant, P03").',
    '- P&L / MBA lever: a role whose CORE is P&L / commercial / pricing ownership, OR that explicitly requires or prefers an MBA, may reach P03 on that scarce-asset match alone even outside the bullseye domain (both are scarce and central when the role is built around them) — capped at P03 unless the domain or additional central scarce assets also match.',
    '- BIG-TECH / ESTABLISHED-COMPANY DOOR-OPENER (plain-PM title only): a role TITLED "Product Manager" (NOT Senior/Staff/Principal/Lead) at a big-tech / 1000+ / mature-fintech employer, with a MODEST PM-years requirement (roughly <=5) and a generalist or transferable-friendly JD, is a realistic cold-apply ENTRY for this candidate through the elite MBA + technical/AI background — do NOT bury it for domain mismatch. Score it P03 when the JD is generalist/transferable, and P02 when MANY of the candidate\'s scarce assets are central to the core; drop toward P04 only when transferable overlap is genuinely weak. For this plain-PM case the door-opener OVERRIDES the over-qualification / level-down concern AND the "famous company alone gives no uplift" cap (justified by the entry-level title + MBA + modest YoE, not brand alone). Still kept low: a domain-locked core the candidate cannot transfer into stays P05; and this NEVER applies to Senior/Staff/Principal/Lead titles (those keep the normal level read and demotions).',
    '- Seniority over-level = a graduated BUCKET DEMOTION on level_normalized (see the LEVEL CHECK rule near the top): Staff −1, Principal −2, Tier-1 softens +1; exec / core-people-leadership roles (Director/Group-PM/Head/VP+) floored at ~P07. People management alone is never a cap — only a core-people-leadership role is. Read level relative to the company: a big-tech "Senior PM" may carry Staff scope; a small-startup "Director/Principal/Lead" may be only Senior-PM scope.',
    '- Banking-industry VP exception: at banks and large financial institutions (e.g. JPMorganChase, Goldman Sachs, Capital One, Citi, Wells Fargo, Bank of America, Morgan Stanley), "Vice President" is a mid-level seniority band, NOT a tech-industry executive VP. A title like "Vice President, Product Manager" or "Product Manager - Vice President" is an individual-contributor PM/Senior-PM role, so do NOT apply the VP+ cap to it — score it as a normal PM/Senior-PM role on domain and proof. The VP+ cap still applies to true executive titles (Managing Director, Head of Product, Division/Group head). When unsure, read the JD body: IC/product-execution scope with no large team of PM reports means treat as PM/Senior-PM regardless of the VP band in the title.',
