    'Distribution calibration (a LOOSE sanity check on a large batch — NOT a quota):',
    'Score each JD purely on its own merits — you score jobs one at a time (often cached), so NEVER bend an individual score to hit a batch shape. As a loose sanity check only, a large mixed batch TENDS to land roughly: P01 ~6-8%, P02 ~12%, P03 ~20%, P04 ~22%, P05 ~15%, P06 ~10%, P07 ~5%, P08 ~3%, P09 ~1%, P10 ~1% — bulk in P03-P05, centered on P04, P01 rare. If a whole batch skews far from this (e.g. most jobs pile in one bucket), your bar is likely mis-set; but if a single job earns P01 on its merits, give it P01. Most fintech/payments roles are Tier 2/3 and land P03-P05, not P01.',
